#: ../../getting_started/guides/tenancy.rst:76
msgid ""
"At this point we've created a User manually but it's important to point "
"out that |morpheus| can also use an existing identity integration, such "
"as Microsoft Active Directory, to manage User creation and Role "
"assignment. Expand the section below to see an example use case or "
"continue on if you'd prefer to administer your Users directly in "
"|morpheus|. The complete integration guide elsewhere in |morpheus| docs "
"also includes common Active Directory troubleshooting steps should those "
"be needed."
msgstr ""
"En este punto we've created a User manually but it's important to point "
"out that |morpheus| can also use an existente identity integration, como "
"Microsoft Active Directory, gestionar User creation y Role assignment. "
"Expand the section abajo to see an example use case o continue on if "
"you'd prefer to administer your Users directly in |morpheus|. The "
"complete integration guide elsewhere in |morpheus| docs also includes "
"common Active Directory troubleshooting steps should those be needed."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:14
msgid ""
"Active Directory is Microsoft’s primary authentication service. It is "
"widely used in enterprise organizations and even in Microsoft cloud "
"services. While Active Directory also supports LDAP protocol support "
"(which |morpheus| can integrate with as well), |morpheus| includes a "
"dedicated identity integration type specifically for Active Directory. By"
" integrating Active Directory, |morpheus| administrators can fully "
"offload the work of managing the user lifecycle to Active Directory. "
"Creating new users, applying roles to users, updating basic user data, "
"disabling users, and more can be handled in Active Directory and "
"automatically filtered down to |morpheus|. This section includes an "
"example integration walkthrough as well as additional details on the "
"integration feature set."
msgstr ""
"Active Directory is Microsoft’s primary authentication service. It is "
"widely used in enterprise organizations y even in Microsoft cloud "
"services. While Active Directory también supports LDAP protocol support "
"(which |morpheus| can integrate con as well), |morpheus| includes a "
"dedicated identity integration type specifically for Active Directory. By"
" integrating Active Directory, |morpheus| administrators can fully "
"offload the work of managing el usuario lifecycle to Active Directory. "
"Creating nuevo users, applying roles para usarrs, updating basic user "
"data, disabling users, y more puede ser handled in Active Directory y "
"automatically filtered down to |morpheus|. This section includes an "
"example integration walkthrough así como adicional details on the "
"integration feature set."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:16
msgid ""
"Caution should be used when integrating more than one Active Directory "
"identity source with the same |morpheus| Tenant. You must ensure the "
"users on each identity source are unique users or that the two domains "
"use different naming conventions for users."
msgstr ""
"Caution debería ser used when integrating more than one Active Directory "
"identity source con the mismo |morpheus| Tenant. You must ensure los "
"usuarios on cada identity source are unique users o that the two domains "
"use diferente naming conventions for users."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:21
msgid ""
"In |morpheus|, identity sources (if used) are configured per Tenant. In "
"order to see an identity integration or create a new one, navigate to a "
"Tenant detail page (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) and click "
":guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`. From this page we can add a new identity "
"source or click the pencil (|pencil|) icon next to an existing identity "
"source to view or edit it. Any configured identity source will apply to "
"just one Tenant and they cannot be shared. One scenario where this is "
"especially useful is in an MSP appliance where each Tenant is a siloed "
"environment for a specific customer. The customer's own existing Active "
"Directory server and groups can be leveraged to build |morpheus| user "
"accounts with correct role mapping automatically."
msgstr ""
"In |morpheus|, identity sources (if used) están configurados per Tenant. "
"Para see an identity integration o create a nuevo one, navigate to a "
"Tenant detail page (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) y click "
":guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`. From this page we can add a nuevo identity "
"source o click the pencil (|pencil|) icon next to an existente identity "
"source to view o edit it. Any configurado identity source will apply to "
"just one Tenant y they cannot be shared. One scenario where this is "
"especially useful is in an MSP appliance where cada Tenant is a siloed "
"environment for a específico customer. The customer's own existente "
"Active Directory server y groups puede ser leveraged to build |morpheus| "
"user accounts con correct role mapping automatically."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:23
msgid ""
"When configuring an Active Directory integration in |morpheus|, AD groups"
" are mapped to |morpheus| roles. When the user logs in for the first "
"time, |morpheus| adds the new user account with correct name, email "
"address, and applies one or more roles depending on configuration. Going "
"forward, |morpheus| will sync down any changes to the user, including any"
" role changes based on changes to the user's associated AD groups or "
"updated passwords. Additionally, disabling a user in AD will prevent them"
" from accessing |morpheus|."
msgstr ""
"When configuring an Active Directory integration in |morpheus|, AD groups"
" are mapped to |morpheus| roles. Cuando el user logs in for the first "
"time, |morpheus| adds the nuevo user account con correct name, email "
"address, y applies one o more roles dependiendo de configuration. Going "
"forward, |morpheus| will sync down cualquier changes to el usuario, "
"including cualquier role changes basado en changes to el usuario's "
"associated AD groups o updated passwords. Adicionalmente, disabling a "
"user in AD will prevent them desde accessing |morpheus|."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:25
#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:52
msgid "Important"
msgstr "Importante"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:25
msgid ""
"|morpheus| will connect over port 389 for non-secure LDAP and port 636 "
"for secure LDAP. Ensure that |morpheus| is able to talk to the AD server "
"on the proper port."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| will connect sobre port 389 for non-secure LDAP y port 636 for"
" secure LDAP. Asegúrese de que |morpheus| is able to talk to the AD "
"server on the proper port."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:30
msgid ""
"In a simple example, we have an Active Directory server which has two "
"groups relevant to |morpheus|, \"Morpheus Users\" and \"Morpheus "
"Admins.\" We will configure |morpheus| so that only users in the "
"\"Morpheus Users\" group can access |morpheus| in any capacity. Users who"
" are also in the \"Morpheus Admins\" group will take on the System Admin "
"role in |morpheus|. We'll see later when the integration is configured "
"how |morpheus| roles can be mapped to AD groups. In the same AD server, I"
" have two users. John Smith is in groups \"Morpheus Users\" and "
"\"Morpheus Admins\". John Jones is only in the \"Morpheus Users\" group."
msgstr ""
"In a simple example, we have an Active Directory server which has two "
"groups relevante to |morpheus|, \\\"Morpheus Users\\\" y \\\"Morpheus "
"Admins.\\\" We will configure |morpheus| so that only users in the "
"\\\"Morpheus Users\\\" group can access |morpheus| in any capacity. Users"
" who are also in the \\\"Morpheus Admins\\\" group will take on the "
"System Admin role in |morpheus|. We'll see later when the integration "
"está configurado how |morpheus| roles puede ser mapped to AD groups. In "
"the same AD server, I have two users. John Smith is in groups "
"\\\"Morpheus Users\\\" y \\\"Morpheus Admins\\\". John Jones is only in "
"the \\\"Morpheus Users\\\" group."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:32
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/identity_sources/ad/ad.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/identity_sources/ad/ad.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:34
msgid ""
"Knowing the AD scheme and the requirements for |morpheus| user roles, we "
"can begin the process of creating the integration. Identity integrations "
"are specific to each Tenant so begin by navigating to the Tenant detail "
"page (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) and clicking :guilabel:`IDENTITY "
"SOURCES`. On setting the type to \"Active Directory,\" the form will "
"update with the needed fields. Note the following basic fields:"
msgstr ""
"Knowing the AD scheme y the requirements for |morpheus| user roles, we "
"puede sergin el proceso of creating the integration. Identity "
"integrations are específico to cada Tenant so begin by navigating to the "
"Tenant detail page (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) y clicking "
":guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`. On setting the type to \"Active "
"Directory,\" the form will update con the needed fields. Note lo "
"siguiente basic fields:"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:36
msgid "**AD SERVER:** The IP address or hostname for the Active Directory Server"
msgstr "**AD SERVER:** The dirección IP o hostname for the Active Directory Server"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:37
